{
  "id": "Compound::DB00720 - Gene::292",
  "verbalization": "Clodronate appears to interact with Slc25a4 through binding, which is linked to the transport of adenine or purine nucleobases across cellular membranes. This interaction is supported by the observed pathway evidence, where Slc25a4 is involved in two distinct membrane transport activities—adenine transmembrane transport and purine nucleobase transmembrane transport. Both of these activities are ultimately linked to Slc25a5, suggesting a potential functional relationship between Clodronate and Slc25a5. The shared involvement of Slc25a4 in these transport processes implies that Clodronate may influence the activity of Slc25a5 through its interaction with Slc25a4. The evidence suggests a possible mechanism where Clodronate modulates the function of Slc25a4, which in turn affects Slc25a5, though the exact nature of this modulation remains to be fully elucidated.",
